Hi all, 

lets say that in the sleepstudy data drivers were measured while sleeping in rooms with another driver. The study was conducted in two different years, and each year drivers were allowed to choose their own partner (they usually changed their partner in the second year). Drivers are not necessarily the same in different years. I want to control for potential effects of the interaction between drivers. What is the correct specification? 

fm1 <- lmer(Reaction ~ 1 + Days + (1 + Days|Subject)+(1|partner_ID), sleepstudy) 

fm2 <- lmer(Reaction ~ 1 + Days + (1 + Days|partner_ID:Subject), sleepstudy) 

fm3 <- lmer(Reaction ~ 1 + Days + (1 + Days|Subject)+(1|partner_ID:Subject), sleepstudy) 


